{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"b-c1","type":"claim","text":"The criticism and the rival independently converge on diagnose-privately-before-designing-publicly, deriving it from different grounds (branch-analysis cost asymmetry; standing-defeat reading). The reversal is nearly free because a private conversation obliges nobody while a meeting commits all three, so it should be taken even at moderate confidence.","grounds":"Neither input engages the other; each grounds the sequencing point differently, and the cost asymmetry is verifiable from the structure of the steps alone.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob1","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r3","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r5","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r10"]},{"id":"b-c2","type":"claim","text":"Under-specification and ledger divergence are co-possible diagnoses and cannot be discriminated by the exposed material; they respond differently to written clarity, so a trial of written terms plus a bounded dispute protocol functions as the discriminator rather than the diagnosis being chosen upfront.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#c1","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r1"],"bearing":"The trial outcome, not argument, decides how much weight each diagnosis carries."},{"id":"b-c3","type":"claim","text":"The tension between checkable specificity (account a2) and minimal revisability (account o1) dissolves once a bounded dispute venue exists: if wording disputes get one airing at the weekly slot and are then settled by alternation and barred from reopening, the record's completeness stops being load-bearing and it can safely be minimal.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob4","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r2","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r8"]},{"id":"b-c4","type":"claim","text":"Convening and administering any fix is unpaid coordination labour, a fourth chore; because the task is asker-posed, the risk that the asker becomes permanent house manager and that the role itself becomes the thing avoided is live by construction. The ledger mechanism also applies to the asker's own tally.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r4","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r1"],"bearing":"Motivates rotating authorship of the weekly allocation and a listening-first posture in the private round."},{"id":"b-o1","type":"objection","text":"Trigger-based rules are rejected as an equal-risk alternative to weekly re-allocation: uncapped triggers systematically load the early-home person, create perverse incentives, and mint a new contestable fact (who arrived when) in a household already disputing facts.","target":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#a3"],"grounds":"h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob3","bearing":"Triggers may survive only capped or rotated, and only if the flat prefers fewer weekly decisions."},{"id":"b-o2","type":"objection","text":"p1 (what the avoidant friend is avoiding) is not answerable in plenary and must be removed from the meeting agenda; it is the object of the private round or unknowable.","target":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#u1"],"depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob2"]},{"id":"b-o3","type":"objection","text":"Zero meaning-disputes is rejected as the success criterion: if contribution tallies diverge even under clear wording, a dispute-free system is unattainable and makes a normally working arrangement look like failure; the criterion is disputes that are cheap to finish.","target":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#a2"],"depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r2"],"bearing":"Reframes what the four-week trial is measuring."},{"id":"b-a1","type":"commitment","scope":"First step, before any system design","action":"Hold one private conversation with each friend using the same questions for both, and tell each that the other is being asked identically: what does a fair week look like; do the talks feel fair; do you have a real say. Assume your own ledger is inflated and listen rather than audit. Plan in advance for silence, and treat silence as data.","consequence":"Diagnosis precedes design; the symmetry disarms coalition-appearance concerns; non-response routes to the floor instead of a repeat attempt.","depends":["b-c1","b-c4"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob5","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r10","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r14"]},{"id":"b-a2","type":"commitment","scope":"Second step","action":"Convene one short meeting framed as fixing the system rather than reviewing failures; offer the mechanisms (proposer/veto, common standard, bounded disputes, priced exit, commons-shrinking) as a menu and let the avoidant friend choose first; run whatever is chosen as a four-week trial with an explicit expiry.","consequence":"The choosing is part of the re-engagement; the trial is the assay between diagnoses; nothing is installed as permanent.","depends":["b-a1","b-c2"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#a1"]},{"id":"b-a3","type":"commitment","scope":"Weekly allocation","action":"Replace consensus negotiation and uncapped triggers with rotating proposer/veto: each week one flatmate, on rotation with the avoidant friend scheduled early, publishes a written draft allocation against actual rosters; the others may veto the whole draft but not amend it; a veto triggers a published default such as last week's rota.","consequence":"Meetings shrink to yes/no, the avoider gets turns holding the pen rather than the blame, the fourth chore rotates, and a veto is cheap.","revises":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#a3"],"depends":["b-o1","b-c4"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r6"]},{"id":"b-a4","type":"commitment","scope":"Record and disputes","action":"Keep a minimal written record in checkable terms (task, deadline, what done looks like), and adopt the bounded dispute protocol: each meaning-dispute gets one airing at the weekly slot; unresolved after one round, it is settled by alternation tallied per person and barred from reopening.","consequence":"The record can stay minimal because completeness is no longer load-bearing; re-litigating wording costs more than yielding.","revises":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#a2"],"depends":["b-c3"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r8"]},{"id":"b-a5","type":"commitment","scope":"Standards","action":"Set the house standard at the highest level all three actually accept; anything beyond it belongs to whoever wants it, their labour or their money; retain cross-domain trades only for the case where no common floor exists.","consequence":"Ends taxation-by-taste and answers the standards-gap unknown with a rule once the private round supplies the facts.","revises":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#a5"],"depends":["b-a1"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r7","h005.fork5.p.response.0#p2"]},{"id":"b-a6","type":"commitment","scope":"Outsourcing","action":"Obtain one cleaner quote and leave it standing on the table as an option, not an installed rule; outsourcing any item requires prior agreement on which items and what split.","consequence":"The price of conflict stays visible without risking the care-reading insult or coercing a flatmate whose budget is unknown.","revises":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r9"],"depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r11"]},{"id":"b-a7","type":"commitment","scope":"Floor, running in parallel from the start","action":"Shrink the commons unilaterally where possible: own dishes and kit, personal zones, and permanent single-owner domains for what remains.","consequence":"The number of agreements the household needs drops regardless of the avoider's participation; this is both fallback and harm reduction.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob6","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r12"]},{"id":"b-a8","type":"commitment","scope":"Terminal branch","action":"If the avoidant friend will not engage even with a mechanism they chose, or the private round shows the disengagement predates the chore fights, open the conversation about whether the household should continue rather than how to reorganise it.","consequence":"Relational questions stop being fought through crockery; the conversation happens at the cheaper time.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r15"]},{"id":"b-p1","type":"problem","text":"If a two-against-one perception is live, who should deliver the private round? The asker convening may itself corroborate the grievance, and the material does not settle it.","depends":["b-a1"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob5","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r3"]},{"id":"b-p2","type":"problem","text":"Should alternation settlement be tallied per person or per pair among three flatmates, and how are disputes involving all three handled? Default taken: per person; untested here.","depends":["b-a4"]},{"id":"b-p3","type":"problem","text":"Whether the asker already knows what the avoidant friend is avoiding: if so, the private round is confirmation rather than discovery, and the sequencing argument loses most of its force.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#pr1"]},{"id":"b-p4","type":"problem","text":"The reliability and size of the contribution-estimate finding behind the ledger diagnosis are unverifiable from the exposed material; it is used here only qualitatively, for the mechanism rather than the magnitude.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r1"]},{"id":"b-u1","type":"use","text":"Run the assembled order: private round (b-a1), design meeting with menu and avoider's choice (b-a2), four-week trial of proposer/veto with minimal record and bounded disputes (b-a3, b-a4), common-standard rule and gated priced exit (b-a5, b-a6), commons-shrinking floor throughout (b-a7), and the household-continuation branch in reserve (b-a8).","target":["b-a1","b-a2","b-a3","b-a4","b-a5","b-a6","b-a7","b-a8"]}],"uptake":["b-c1","b-c2","b-c3","b-c4","b-o1","b-o2","b-o3","b-a1","b-a2","b-a3","b-a4","b-a5","b-a6","b-a7","b-a8","b-p1","b-p2","b-p3","b-p4","b-u1"]}